prompt take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first on the Rye-first crypto parity road; Rye prioritized, Glow on green-witnessed Rye; approve own design rounds; send each finished increment as its own signed round; stop at custody gates; baton prin recur
think Read the road-ahead trio (1024-round itinerary, six-season double-seat, the Aug-15 decision wave) plus REMEMBER's living Git-nib line. The living metal-producing thread is Season G crypto; the decision wave names the wallet arc's next rung outright — "next the wallet arc is BIP-39 entropy→mnemonic then BIP-44 account paths." Entropy→mnemonic landed last commit (993076ea2c), so the Lindy-first crux-first lap is BIP-44 account paths.
think Lindy weight is high — BIP-44 is the convention every wallet in the world reads a derivation path by, so the tree's own wallet reaches the same address for the same phrase; it serves every future signing surface (Kumara, Lotus carry, Vault). Crux weight is right — it is the hardest-solvable next wallet-arc rung that is still a pure composition: a path grammar over the already-GREEN bip32, authoring NO new cryptography.
think Chose the self-contained, no-fetch parity anchor: BIP-32's OWN published Test Vector 1 (seed 000102…0f) walks the mixed hardened/normal path m/0'/1/2'/2/1000000000 — exactly what a path parser walks. bip32.rye already holds those six nodes' xprv/xpub char-for-char, so walking each node BY ITS HUMAN PATH STRING and reproducing the spec's published strings proves the parser, the hardened marker, and the walk against a real standard answer with zero external dependency.
think Authored crypto/bip44.rye: parse_path reads "m/44'/60'/0'/0/0"-style text into the exact 32-bit index list (the ' / h / H marker sets the hardened bit; decimal accumulation kept overflow-safe entirely in u32 with a guard before the multiply and before the add, so a bare index can never wrap or reach 2³¹); derive_path parses then walks bip32.ckd_priv from master_from_seed; derive_bip44 builds the five-level path directly from coin_type/account/change/address_index with the top three levels hardened. Named BIP-44 constants (purpose 44, coin_type_bitcoin 0, coin_type_ethereum 60, change external/internal) rather than magic numbers. Every width named; contract asserts on parse depth and the walk bound; named errors BadPath/IndexTooLarge/PathTooDeep.
obs GREEN on the FIRST metal build — no reds. Parity holds four ways: all six BIP-32 Test Vector 1 nodes walked by their human path strings serialize to EXACTLY the spec's published xprv AND xpub; m/44'/60'/0'/0/0 parses to [44+H, 60+H, 0+H, 0, 0] and m/44'/0'/0'/1/5 to [44+H, 0+H, 0+H, 1, 5] (h/H harden as ' does); derive_bip44 and derive_path reach the same account leaf byte-for-byte, serialized as a well-formed xprv; and the edges refuse — empty path, no master, a non-digit index, an index at 2³¹ (with 2³¹-1 accepted as the largest legal bare index), a too-deep path, and a trailing slash each raise their named error. TAME style bans clean.
obs Registered after bip39_mnemonic in the suite — the count-guard bijection now prints 49 (thirty-five primitives + fourteen compositions, bip44 the fourteenth composition). Synced crypto/README.md and docs/CRYPTO.md front-door counts 48→49 and 13→14 compositions, added a rung row to each, and fixed the suite's own GREEN prose line, which was stale at forty-seven while the true count had already reached forty-eight before this lap. Every key is a TEST key from the spec's own seed; generating a real wallet and signing with its key stays the custody gate (#3/#4). Purely local — no network, no funds, no device.
